You are a logic expert.

Given the following premises and a conclusion, determine whether the conclusion logically follows from the premises.

Premises:
(forall x (RomanceLanguage(x) -> IndoEuropeanLanguage(x))) AND (forall x (RomanceLanguage(x) -> MemberOf(x, languageFamily))) AND (forall x forall y forall z ((MemberOf(x, z) AND MemberOf(y, z)) -> (Related(x, y) AND Related(y, x)))) AND (RomanceLanguage(french) AND RomanceLanguage(spanish)) AND (Related(german, spanish)) AND (forall x (Language(x) -> NOT Related(basque, x)))

Conclusion:
IndoEuropeanLanguage(french)

Put your final answer within \boxed{True}, \boxed{False}, or \boxed{Uncertain}.<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>


